  to their spoken language, with English-speaking Mexican-Americans of all ages more likely to report tobacco, alcohol  
  or illicit drug use than were corresponding Spanish-speaking Mexican-Americans. Awareness of the racial/ethnic and    
  age differences in the rates of tobacco, alcohol and illicit drug use will assist physicians in the early             
